在M40高速上开着车，突然遇到个颠簸……（拟声）
Driving down the M40,
here's a hump... (VOCALISES)

260
00:13:43,133 --> 00:13:44,667
“我掉出车外了！”
"I've fallen out!"

261
00:13:44,700 --> 00:13:47,433
那是你自己操作失误，
又不是开汽车必须经历的。
That's user error,
it's not obligatory.

262
00:13:47,467 --> 00:13:48,800
-我能换个话题了吗？
-哈蒙德：赶紧的，拜托了。
-Can I just move it on?
-HAMMOND: Yes, please.

263
00:13:48,833 --> 00:13:51,767
这周我听了个特有意思的事。
你们知道Travelodge连锁酒店吧？
Heard a great story this week.
You know Travelodge?

264
00:13:51,800 --> 00:13:54,933
就那帮……开在路边的快捷小旅馆。
The people... Little hotels
at the side of the road.

265
00:13:54,967 --> 00:13:58,567
他们最近决定把房间腾出来，
They've decided that now
they will open up their rooms,

266
00:13:58,667 --> 00:14:02,967
每次按半小时出租给开累了的司机休息。
rent them for half an hour
at a time to tired motorists.

267
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:05,167
-大白天的。
-（观众笑声）
-During the day.
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

268
00:14:07,033 --> 00:14:08,100
只要五镑钱。
For a fiver.

269
00:14:08,133 --> 00:14:09,800
要是有一位男司机
和一位女司机，
So a gentleman
and a lady motorist

270
00:14:09,833 --> 00:14:11,933
决定顺道去“歇息”片刻……
decide they need a little bit
of a break...

271
00:14:11,967 --> 00:14:14,800
-我立马跟你想到一块儿去了。
-“打个盹”！
-I immediately thought
the same as you.
-Little nap!

272
00:14:14,833 --> 00:14:16,400
一对男女车主正开着车，
A gentleman
and a lady motorist
are driving along

273
00:14:16,433 --> 00:14:17,933
突然说：咱去“打个盹”吧。
and say let's have a "nap".

274
00:14:19,400 --> 00:14:21,233
去Travelodge旅馆，花五镑睡半小时。
For half an hour, for a fiver,
in the Travelodge.

275
00:14:21,267 --> 00:14:25,367
但想得美，人家其实规定了，
房间仅限单人入住。
But no, they're actually
saying the rooms
are only single occupancy.

276
00:14:25,400 --> 00:14:28,200
只准你自己一个人进去。
They'll only allow you
in there on your own.

277
00:14:28,233 --> 00:14:30,667
那你一个人进去打什么盹啊？
So why would you want
to have a nap?

278
00:14:30,667 --> 00:14:35,100
“我刚看了眼帕米拉·安德森的照片，
现在急需去‘打个盹’……”
I've just been looking at this
picture of Pamela Anderson
and I need a nap...

279
00:14:37,700 --> 00:14:39,367
五分钟完事。
For five minutes.

280
00:14:39,400 --> 00:14:43,100
那么，想象一下某天你正在开车，
Now, imagine
you're driving along one day,

281
00:14:43,133 --> 00:14:46,467
然后突然之间，
你就一头栽进了湖里。
and suddenly
you veer off into a lake.

282
00:14:46,500 --> 00:14:48,400
这事儿真会发生。没开玩笑。
It does happen. Seriously.

283
00:14:49,733 --> 00:14:51,433
真的会发生，说正经的。
It does happen. Seriously.

284
00:14:51,467 --> 00:14:57,200
在英国，每年淹死在车里的人，
比在人工划船湖里淹死的还要多。
Every year in Britain
more people drown in cars
than on boating lakes.

285
00:14:57,233 --> 00:15:00,700
千真万确。
所以，我决定……
It's absolutely true.
So, I decided...

286
00:15:00,733 --> 00:15:03,033
好吧，其实是杰里米
和詹姆斯决定的——
Well, Jeremy
and James decided

287
00:15:03,067 --> 00:15:07,200
让我把自己淹一次，
来好好调查这回事。
that I should investigate this
by drowning myself.

288
00:15:07,233 --> 00:15:09,867
哈蒙德：首先，
特技指导
肖恩·罗杰斯
HAMMOND: First,
stunt coordinator
Sean Rogers

289
00:15:09,900 --> 00:15:11,700
把我拉到一边，
悄悄交代了几句。
took me aside
for a quiet word.

290
00:15:11,733 --> 00:15:13,267
这不是为了吓你。
This is not to scare you.

291
00:15:13,300 --> 00:15:16,233
只是想让你看看
这车灌满水能有多快。
It's just to show you
how quickly this car
could fill up.

292
00:15:16,267 --> 00:15:17,433
明白吗？
All right?

293
00:15:23,567 --> 00:15:25,867
（机械运转摩擦声）
(MECHANISM GRINDS)

294
00:15:29,800 --> 00:15:31,433
哈蒙德：好的。
HAMMOND: Okay.

295
00:15:31,467 --> 00:15:35,500
要是你光顾着愣神，水就会这样灌进来，
一直灌进来……
If you wait, we're talking
about the water coming in,
coming in...

296
00:15:39,467 --> 00:15:41,967
-这就完事了。
-彻底沉下去了。
-And that's it.
-Now it's gone.

297
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:44,400
-真够快的，对吧？
-一点没错。
-That's quick, isn't it?
-That's right.

298
00:15:44,433 --> 00:15:47,733
所以你根本没闲工夫瞎磨蹭。
So you haven't got time
to muck about.

299
00:15:47,767 --> 00:15:52,667
哈蒙德：显然，直接把车开进湖里
HAMMOND: Now, obviously,
it isn't a good idea to simply
drive a car into a lake

300
00:15:52,667 --> 00:15:54,233
瞧瞧会发生什么，绝不是明智之举。
and see what happens.

301
00:15:54,267 --> 00:15:57,967
所以，我们准备了一个大水箱，还有几位安全潜水员。
Instead, we've got ourselves
a tank and some safety divers.

302
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:02,200
现在，我唯一要做的
就是学点基础潜水技巧，
Now, all I need to do
is learn some basic
diving techniques,

303
00:16:02,233 --> 00:16:04,200
以防真闹出什么岔子。
just in case things go wrong.

304
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:11,967
在动真格上演特技之前，
Before we did
the stunt for real,

305
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:15,667
我得潜到水下
去练习应急手势信号，
I had to go underwater
to practise the emergency
hand signals,

306
00:16:15,667 --> 00:16:19,433
万一出了状况，
潜水员好及时给我供气。
in case there was a problem
and the divers had
to give me air.

307
00:16:22,500 --> 00:16:24,667
然后，为了再添点刺激感，
Then, just to spice things
up a bit,

308
00:16:24,700 --> 00:16:27,667
他们毫无预警地扯掉了我的面罩。
they ripped my face mask off
without warning.

309
00:16:34,867 --> 00:16:39,300
果不其然，
没过几秒，
我就灌了一大口水。
And sure enough,
within seconds,
I was breathing water.

310
00:16:39,333 --> 00:16:40,967
这开局可不太妙。
Not a good start.

311
00:16:43,500 --> 00:16:46,433
紧接着，为了给我极可能遭受的工伤
再添点精神羞辱，
And then to add insult
to my likely injuries,

312
00:16:46,467 --> 00:16:49,533
我第一次见到了
我未来的“专属棺材”。
I got first sight
of my potential coffin.

313
00:16:49,567 --> 00:16:53,700
一辆老掉牙的F牌沃克斯豪尔Carlton，
甚至连GSi都不是。
An F-reg Vauxhall Carlton.
Not even a GSI.

314
00:16:54,500 --> 00:16:55,967
呵，真是谢谢你们了啊。
Oh, thank you.

315
00:16:57,333 --> 00:16:59,800
随着实测的时刻越来越近，
As the time approached
to actually do this,

316
00:16:59,833 --> 00:17:05,100
虽然我知道身边围了一大群安全保障人员
确保我死不了，
even though I knew I had
a host of safety people around
me to make sure I was okay,

317
00:17:05,133 --> 00:17:08,400
但我不得不承认，
我的神经已经紧绷到了极点。
I've got to confess,
my nerves were on edge.

318
00:17:09,833 --> 00:17:12,800
好吧，我现在正悬在水面上晃悠……
Okay, I'm swinging
above the water...

319
00:17:14,233 --> 00:17:15,500
坐在车里。
In a car.

320
00:17:17,700 --> 00:17:20,400
眼看就要大难临头了。
About to have
a horrible accident.

321
00:17:28,033 --> 00:17:29,200
真正的恐惧。
Real fear.

322
00:17:31,067 --> 00:17:32,533
一种实打实的恐惧感。
A real sense of fear.

323
00:17:34,833 --> 00:17:36,167
好吧。
Okay.

324
00:17:36,200 --> 00:17:38,667
-罗杰斯：理查德，
你还好吗？
-我还好。
-ROGERS: Richard,
are you okay?
-I'm okay.

325
00:17:40,300 --> 00:17:42,067
-罗杰斯：准备好了吗，弗雷德？
-好了。
-ROGERS: Ready, Fred?
-Ready.

326
00:17:42,100 --> 00:17:43,567
罗杰斯：潜水员，准备好了吗？
ROGERS: Divers, ready?

327
00:17:45,100 --> 00:17:46,833
罗杰斯：好的，各就各位。
ROGERS: Okay, standby.

328
00:17:46,867 --> 00:17:48,967
五，四，
Five, four,

329
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:52,667
三，二，一，开拍！
three, two, one, action!

330
00:17:56,667 --> 00:18:00,133
至于我会不会死，
咱们待会儿见分晓。
And we'll find out later
if I die.

331
00:18:00,167 --> 00:18:01,933
但首先，
But first,

332
00:18:01,967 --> 00:18:05,100
咱们又迎来了一辆
捷豹概念车。
here's yet another
Jaguar concept car.

333
00:18:06,067 --> 00:18:08,067
这台叫做 R-D6。
This one is called the R-D6.

334
00:18:08,100 --> 00:18:11,667
通体几乎全是用铝打造的，
轻得出奇。
It's made almost entirely
of aluminium.
It's very light.

335
00:18:11,700 --> 00:18:16,567
更让人不可思议的是，它居然搭载了一台
V6 涡轮增压柴油发动机。
And it's powered, remarkably,
by a turbo-charged,
V6 diesel engine.

336
00:18:16,667 --> 00:18:19,533
我最中意的其实是内饰，
瞧瞧这个。
The bit I really like
is the inside.
Have a look at this.

337
00:18:19,567 --> 00:18:21,167
仔细看看这里。
黑色真皮，
Now have a look at that.
Black leather,

338
00:18:21,200 --> 00:18:25,033
那些锃亮的部件，
还有脚坑里泛着的红光。
all those shiny bits
and those red lights
down the footwell.

339
00:18:25,067 --> 00:18:29,100
很显然，某位捷豹设计师
在伏特加酒吧里喝得烂醉如泥，
Now, clearly a Jaguar designer
got completely lashed
in a vodka bar

340
00:18:29,133 --> 00:18:31,233
然后脑子一热：“得嘞，我就给它整成这副模样吧。”
and thought, "I'll make it
look like this then."

341
00:18:31,267 --> 00:18:33,533
所以车门边八成还得配个看门保镖，
So, obviously there will
be a bouncer on the door,

342
00:18:33,567 --> 00:18:36,467
拦着你告诉你穿运动鞋免进。
telling you you can't come in
because you got trainers on.

343
00:18:36,500 --> 00:18:38,767
这车长相确实惊艳，
It's a gorgeous looking thing,

344
00:18:38,800 --> 00:18:42,000
但这正是我对捷豹概念车
百思不得其解的地方。
but here's the thing
I don't get about
Jaguar concept cars.

345
00:18:42,033 --> 00:18:45,667
两年前，差不多那时候吧，
他们展示了 XK180。
Two years ago, about then,
they showed us the XK180.

346
00:18:45,667 --> 00:18:50,767
就是它，当时说是为了展示
未来的捷豹会长成什么样。
And there it is, that was
to show us what Jaguars
of the future will look like.

347
00:18:50,800 --> 00:18:54,000
结果到了去年，
他们又造了个 R-Coupe，
But then last year,
they did the R-Coupe,

348
00:18:54,033 --> 00:18:57,433
说是为了展示未来的捷豹长成什么样。
to show us what Jaguars
of the future will look like.

349
00:18:57,467 --> 00:19:00,100
现在他们又卷土重来，
整了这么个玩意儿，好向我们展示
Now they're back again
with this to show us

350
00:19:00,133 --> 00:19:03,833
未来的捷豹会长成什么样。
what Jaguars of the future
will look like.

351
00:19:03,867 --> 00:19:06,667
我说捷豹啊，
你的意思大家都懂了。
Now look, Jaguar,
you have made your point.

352
00:19:07,267 --> 00:19:08,867
赶紧把车造出来得了！
Just make the car!

353
00:19:09,800 --> 00:19:11,700
好了，来见见本期的嘉宾。
Right, let's meet
this week's guest.

354
00:19:11,733 --> 00:19:14,000
他是个演员，也是个喜剧明星，
He's an actor,
he's a comedian,

355
00:19:14,033 --> 00:19:17,933
代表作是《马里昂与杰夫》，我简直爱死这戏了，
绝妙的电视节目。
he's responsible for Marion
and Geoff, which I just love,
terrific television programme.

356
00:19:17,967 --> 00:19:20,800
如果我没记错的话，
翻翻看以往记录，
And if we look down here,
I think I'm right in saying

357
00:19:20,833 --> 00:19:22,733
他还是我们节目请来的首位威尔士人。
he's the first Welshman
we've ever had on.

358
00:19:22,767 --> 00:19:25,267
女士们，先生们，
罗伯·布莱顿！
Ladies and gentlemen,
Rob Brydon!

359
00:19:25,300 --> 00:19:26,767
（观众欢呼）
(AUDIENCE CHEERING)

360
00:19:28,933 --> 00:19:31,967
-杰里米！
-你好啊？请坐。
-Jeremy!
-All right? Take a seat.

361
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:33,000
你好！
Hello!

362
00:19:36,700 --> 00:19:38,733
克拉克森：那么，呃……
CLARKSON: So, um...

363
00:19:38,767 --> 00:19:42,567
我们都知道，世界上所有重要的一切
几乎都是苏格兰人发明的。
Now, we know the Scottish have
given us really everything
that matters in the world.

364
00:19:42,667 --> 00:19:44,233
没错。
Yes.

365
00:19:44,267 --> 00:19:46,033
要是说威尔士人什么都没贡献，
未免有点太刻薄了。
And it would be cheap to say
the Welsh have given
us nothing.

366
00:19:46,667 --> 00:19:47,867
又来了。是的。
Here we go. Yes.

367
00:19:47,900 --> 00:19:49,767
不，说真的，因为我们刚才琢磨了一下，
No, really, because we were
working it out

368
00:19:49,800 --> 00:19:53,267
威尔士人其实为戏剧界
贡献了所有大腕。
and really the Welsh have
given the theatre everybody.

369
00:19:53,300 --> 00:19:57,267
-伯顿、泽塔-琼斯、霍普金斯。
-对，但是，但是，但是……
-Burton. Zeta-Jones. Hopkins.
-Yes, but, but, but...

370
00:19:57,300 --> 00:20:01,367
你看，你把那些真正的大腕给忘了，
那些戏剧媒体界的超级大腕。
You see, you forget
the big names, the big
theatrical media names.

371
00:20:01,400 --> 00:20:03,167
比如气象女主播夏恩·劳埃德。
Sian Lloyd, the weather girl.

372
00:20:03,900 --> 00:20:05,667
对，她算一个……
Yeah, she's...

373
00:20:05,700 --> 00:20:08,367
-还有Steps乐队的H。
-他也是威尔士人？
-H from Steps.
-Is he Welsh as well?

374
00:20:08,400 --> 00:20:12,567
我觉得H那家伙，现在在北威尔士老家
弄了个微缩版的“猫王雅园”，
I think H actually,
he's got a mini Graceland
now up in North Wales,

375
00:20:12,600 --> 00:20:13,967
就在他老家那块儿。
where he comes from.

376
00:20:14,000 --> 00:20:16,933
一年下来能吸引多达六七个游客呢。
And they get up to six
or seven visitors a year.

377
00:20:16,967 --> 00:20:18,800
（观众大笑）
(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

378
00:20:18,833 --> 00:20:21,000
这真是不可思议，想想那些伟大的演出，
It is an astonishing thing,
when you think about
the great performances,

379
00:20:21,033 --> 00:20:22,500
那是国家剧院里的霍普金斯，
it is Hopkins at the National,

380
00:20:22,533 --> 00:20:25,500
还有老维克剧院里的伯顿，诸如此类的。
and it is Burton
at the Old Vic, whatever.

381
00:20:25,533 --> 00:20:29,133
至于你，好像没怎么去过那些高雅殿堂吧？
You, not really been there,
have you?

382
00:20:29,167 --> 00:20:32,767
你更出名的身份，
是给汽车广告配音。
You're more famous
for your car advertisement
voice-overs.

383
00:20:33,733 --> 00:20:34,967
可不是嘛！
He is!

384
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:38,000
每次你在电视上听到汽车广告，
Every time you hear a car
advert on the television,

385
00:20:38,033 --> 00:20:41,667
我几乎敢打包票，那声音绝对是他。
I can pretty much guarantee
he is the voice.

386
00:20:41,700 --> 00:20:45,200
你到底配了多少个？福特蒙迪欧那个《猫和老鼠》的广告，就是你配的。
How many have you done?
There's the Ford Mondeo
Tom and Jerry, that was you.

387
00:20:45,233 --> 00:20:47,300
-我觉得那个现在还在播呢，对，是的。
-现在还在播。
-I think that's still running,
yeah. Yeah.
-That's still running.

388
00:20:47,333 --> 00:20:51,300
-还有哪些来着？
-目前好像还有雷诺风景。
-What were the other ones?
-I think the Renault Scenic,
at the moment.

389
00:20:51,333 --> 00:20:52,933
那个广告词是怎么念的？
How does that one go?

390
00:20:52,967 --> 00:20:54,133
（笑）
(LAUGHS)

391
00:20:54,167 --> 00:20:55,267
我都给忘了。
I've forgotten it.

392
00:20:55,300 --> 00:20:56,367
好，你们大家都安静一下，准备好了吗？
Okay, you have to quiet
for it, ready?

393
00:20:56,400 --> 00:20:58,167
（清嗓子）
(CLEARS THROAT)

394
00:20:58,200 --> 00:21:00,200
在最近的欧洲NCAP碰撞测试中，
In the recent NCAP Euro
crash tests,

395
00:21:00,233 --> 00:21:04,200
同级别车型中仅有一款荣获五星安全认证……
only one car in its class
got five stars for safety...

396
00:21:04,233 --> 00:21:06,200
全新雷诺风景。
The new Renault Scenic.

397
00:21:06,967 --> 00:21:08,167
就是他！
It's him!

